<quiz>
  <question type="stack">
    <name>
      <text>Forming and solving a compound inequality for a greenhouse temperature range</text>
    </name>
    <questiontext format="html">
      <text><![CDATA[<p>{@fname@}, a farmer in {@place@}, needs to keep the indoor temperature (\(T\)) of a greenhouse such that it is strictly greater than <b>\({@L@}^\circ\text{C}\)</b> and less than or equal to <b>\({@U@}^\circ\text{C}\)</b>.</p>

<p>Because the greenhouse traps the sun's heat, the air inside is always <b>\({@H@}^\circ\text{C}\) warmer</b> than the air outside. If the outdoor temperature is \(t\), then \(T = t + {@H@}\).</p>

<p>By substituting \(T\) into the compound inequality, determine the range of outdoor temperatures (\(t\)) that keep the greenhouse within this range.</p>
<p><i>(Enter the lower and upper bounds of \(t\) in the boxes below.)</i></p>

<p>[[input:ans1]] \( < t \le \) [[input:ans2]]  [[validation:ans1]] [[feedback:prt1]]  [[validation:ans2]] [[feedback:prt2]]</p>]]></text>
    </questiontext>
    <generalfeedback format="html">
      <text><![CDATA[<h3>Worked Solution:</h3>

<p>First, we translate the initial temperature constraints into a single compound inequality. The indoor temperature \(T\) must be greater than \({@L@}\) and less than or equal to \({@U@}\):</p>
<p style="margin-left: 20px;">
\( \displaystyle {@L@} < T \le {@U@} \)
</p>

<p>Next, we substitute the expression for the indoor temperature (\(T = t + {@H@}\)) into the middle of the inequality:</p>
<p style="margin-left: 20px;">
\( \displaystyle {@L@} < t + {@H@} \le {@U@} \)
</p>

<p>To isolate the outdoor temperature \(t\), we subtract \({@H@}\) from all three parts of the inequality:</p>
<p style="margin-left: 20px;">
\( \displaystyle \begin{aligned}
{@L@} - {@H@} &< t \le {@U@} - {@H@} \\
{@ta1@} &< t \le {@ta2@}
\end{aligned} \)
</p>

<p>Hence, the required range for the outdoor temperature is:</p>
<p style="margin-left: 20px;">
\( \displaystyle \boxed{{@ta1@} < t \le {@ta2@}} \)
</p>
<div style="text-align:center;" role="img" aria-label="Number line: open circle at {#ta1#}, closed circle at {#ta2#}, shaded between.">
[[jsxgraph width="420px" height="110px"]]
(function() {
  var lo = Math.floor({#ta1#}) - 2, hi = Math.ceil({#ta2#}) + 2, P = [[{#ta1#},{#ta2#},false,true]];
  var b = JXG.JSXGraph.initBoard(divid, {boundingbox:[lo - 0.5, 1.6, hi + 0.5, -1.4], axis:false, grid:false,
      showNavigation:false, showCopyright:false, pan:{enabled:false}, zoom:{enabled:false}});
  b.create('arrow', [[lo - 0.4, 0], [hi + 0.4, 0]], {strokeColor:'#333', fixed:true});
  var step = (hi - lo) > 24 ? 5 : ((hi - lo) > 12 ? 2 : 1);
  for (var t = Math.ceil(lo/step)*step; t <= hi; t += step) {
    b.create('segment', [[t, -0.15], [t, 0.15]], {strokeColor:'#333', fixed:true});
    b.create('text', [t, -0.6, '' + t], {anchorX:'middle', fontSize:12, fixed:true});
  }
  for (var i = 0; i < P.length; i++) {
    var a = P[i][0], c = P[i][1], y = 0.55;
    var x1 = (a === null) ? lo - 0.3 : a, x2 = (c === null) ? hi + 0.3 : c;
    if (a === null) b.create('arrow', [[x2, y], [x1, y]], {strokeColor:'#1565c0', strokeWidth:4, fixed:true});
    else if (c === null) b.create('arrow', [[x1, y], [x2, y]], {strokeColor:'#1565c0', strokeWidth:4, fixed:true});
    else b.create('segment', [[x1, y], [x2, y]], {strokeColor:'#1565c0', strokeWidth:4, fixed:true});
    if (a !== null) b.create('point', [a, y], {name:'', size:5, fixed:true, strokeColor:'#1565c0', strokeWidth:2,
        fillColor: P[i][2] ? '#1565c0' : '#ffffff', showInfobox:false});
    if (c !== null) b.create('point', [c, y], {name:'', size:5, fixed:true, strokeColor:'#1565c0', strokeWidth:2,
        fillColor: P[i][3] ? '#1565c0' : '#ffffff', showInfobox:false});
  }
})();
[[/jsxgraph]]
</div>]]></text>
